# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
/target/

# Remove Cargo.lock from gitignore if creating an executable, leave it for libraries
# More information here https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/cargo-toml-vs-cargo-lock.html
Cargo.lock

# ...but pkcore-perf ships an executable, and a benchmark harness needs a
# pinned dependency graph: version drift silently changes the numbers it
# publishes. See the perf/ layout in
# docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-30-kernel-performance-harness-design.md.
!perf/Cargo.lock

# The global gitignore carries a bare `bin` rule, which matches a directory
# named `bin` at any depth — so without these two lines git never descends
# into perf/src/bin/ and the perf runner binary is silently uncommittable.
# The directory must be re-included before the file: git will not re-include
# a path whose parent directory is excluded.
!perf/src/bin/
!perf/src/bin/*.rs

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk


# Added by cargo

/target
/Cargo.lock

# Added by the author
.env
/mutants.out

# cargo-llvm-cov: `cargo llvm-cov report --lcov` writes here by default (the CI
# coverage job and any local run). The HTML report lands under /target, already
# ignored above. coverage-summary.txt, coverage-html.tar.gz, and release-body.md
# are additional root-level outputs from the release workflow's coverage and
# release-notes steps (see .github/workflows/release.yml), runner-only today
# but ignored so reproducing those steps locally doesn't leave untracked noise.
/lcov.info
/coverage-summary.txt
/coverage-html.tar.gz
/release-body.md
marathon_failure.yaml

graphify-out/
.claude/dog-mode
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# The global gitignore excludes `.claude/` wholesale, which silently drops this
# repo's project-local skills (defect-report, audit-release, release-notes).
# They encode this project's conventions and belong in version control, so
# re-include the directory — git cannot re-include a path whose parent
# directory is excluded, hence the directory line before the contents line.
!.claude/
!.claude/skills/**

# PokerBench dataset (EPIC-43): downloaded at eval time, not committed.
# Tiny vendored samples live under src/pokerbench/fixtures/ instead.
/data/pokerbench/

# wasm
*.wat